spec: S02-03, S02-04, S02-07, S02-15

`push --doc` binds a file to an existing Document (by Name or by the path of a pulled file);
a Sidecar from another Document needs `--force`; the Sidecar is written for an unbound file;
pushing under a new filename renames (Names are recorded per Version).

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push bind-a.md
bind-a	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push bind-b.md
bind-b	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push bind-b.md --doc bind-a
? 5
error: bind-b.md is bound to [..] (bind-b.annotary) — pass --force to rebind it to [..] — or delete the Sidecar to create a new Document

$ annotary -p rowan push bind-b.md --doc bind-a --force
warning: rebinding bind-b.md from [..] to [..]
bind-b	[..]	v2

$ annotary -p rowan versions bind-b.md --json number,name
[{"number":1,"name":"bind-a"},{"number":2,"name":"bind-b"}]

$ annotary -p rowan push unbound/bind-c.md --doc bind-b.md
bind-c	[..]	v3

$ annotary -p rowan status unbound/bind-c.md
bind-c	[..]	v3	action:-	open:0	mentions-me:0	seq:[..]

$ annotary -p rowan push unbound/bind-c.md
bind-c	[..]	already v3

$ annotary -p rowan pull unbound/bind-c.md --version 1 --out v1
pull: 0 threads, 0 assets
(name on v1 was "bind-a"; Threads as they were on v1; head is v3)
bind-a.md	bind-a.annotary	v1

$ annotary -p rowan status v1/bind-a.md
bind-c	[..]	v3	action:-	open:0	mentions-me:0	seq:[..]

```
